  === gate_bribed

  You produce your coin purse with a knowing smile, letting it jingle significantly. "Perhaps I was mistaken about the invitation," you say smoothly. "But I've come a long way, and I'm sure the Archmage wouldn't want to turn away someone who appreciates the... financial realities... of guard duty."

  You pass fifty gold pieces to the taller guard, who palms them expertly. His companion looks away, pretending not to notice.

  "Alright, 'Professor,'" the guard says with a smirk that suggests he knows exactly what you are. "But if anyone asks, you never came through this gate. And if I hear any alarms, we never met. Understood?"

  You nod and slip inside. The guard wasn't wrong to be suspicious—but suspicion without proof means little.

