  === eastern_wall_climb

  You move silently along the tower's perimeter until you reach the eastern face. Here, centuries of weather have worn the stonework, creating handholds and cracks that a skilled climber can exploit. Your climbing gear includes rope, pitons, and padded gloves.

  The wall rises thirty feet to a narrow window on the second floor. You can see faint light within—someone's awake, or perhaps magic illuminates the room constantly. The ascent will be treacherous in the dark, but guards patrol the base of the wall every quarter-hour.

  You wait for the patrol to pass, then begin your climb.

