  === observatory_entrance

  You insert both keys into their respective locks. The wards flare once, blindingly bright, then dissolve like morning mist. The door swings open silently, revealing the tower's pinnacle.

  The observatory is a hemisphere of glass and starlight. At its center, Thessalon stands within a circle of power, arms raised, chanting words that make reality shiver. Before him, suspended in mid-air, floats the Tear of Luminous.

  But it's not a gem. It's an eye—massive, lidless, filled with swirling darkness and distant stars. It stares at nothing and everything, and when your gaze meets it, you feel your sanity begin to fray.

  Thessalon hasn't noticed you yet, consumed by his ritual. The eye pulses in time with his chanting. You can see cracks forming in its surface—whatever is imprisoned within is about to break free.

